@startuml 05-client-sync-state
title Protocol 05 - Client sync state machine (SyncEngine)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

[*] --> Unpaired

state "Unpaired" as Unpaired
state "Pairing" as Pairing
state "Idle" as Idle
state "Pulling" as Pulling
state "Pushing" as Pushing
state "Backoff" as Backoff
state "Offline" as Offline
state "Resyncing" as Resyncing
state "AuthFailed" as AuthFailed

Unpaired --> Pairing : user starts setup or pairing
Pairing --> Unpaired : expired, cancelled\nor key unwrap failed
Pairing --> Pulling : token and account key stored

Idle --> Pulling : poll timer, event "changed",\napp start or wake, local change
Pulling --> Pulling : has_more = true
Pulling --> Pushing : has_more = false\nand outbox not empty
Pulling --> Idle : has_more = false\nand outbox empty
Pushing --> Pushing : outbox not empty
Pushing --> Idle : outbox empty

Pulling --> Backoff : 429, 5xx, timeout
Pushing --> Backoff : 429, 5xx, timeout
Backoff --> Pulling : delay elapsed

Pulling --> Offline : no network
Pushing --> Offline : no network
Idle --> Offline : network lost
Offline --> Pulling : network available

Pulling --> Resyncing : 410 cursor_expired
Resyncing --> Pushing : full pull done,\nlocal store reconciled
Resyncing --> Backoff : 429, 5xx, timeout

Pulling --> AuthFailed : 401
Pushing --> AuthFailed : 401
Resyncing --> AuthFailed : 401
AuthFailed --> Pairing : user pairs again

note right of Idle
  Local edits always succeed, in every state.
  They go to the local store and the outbox.
  Sync is never on the path of a keystroke.
end note

note right of Backoff
  delay = min(15 min, 2 s * 2^attempt) with jitter.
  Retry-After from the server overrides it.
  attempt resets after one successful request.
end note

note left of AuthFailed
  Local notes stay readable and editable.
  The outbox is kept and pushed after re-pairing.
end note

note left of Pulling
  A pull always runs before a push,
  so the device merges remote changes
  before it uploads its own.
end note

@enduml
